 "result": "`tessel routes` is implemented by `routes_command` in `src/tessel/cli.py:1047-1106`. It is registered as a default command on `TesselGroup`.\n\n**Sorting:**\n- `--sort/-s` takes `endpoint` (default), `methods`, `domain`, `rule` or `match`.\n- It builds a `sorts` list that mirrors the column order: `endpoint`, `methods`, then `domain` (only if any rule has a host/subdomain), then `rule`.\n- `rows.sort(key=itemgetter(sorts.index(sort)))` sorts the rows by the column matching that name.\n- `match` isn't in `sorts`, so `.index()` raises `ValueError`, which is caught and ignored. Rows then stay in `url_map.iter_rules()` order, which is the order Tessel matches routes.\n- `domain` with no host/subdomain column also hits the `ValueError`, so rows are left unsorted.",
